			            The same Individual applies again for
			            <b>Community Friend in 2026</b>:
			            <b>Returning</b>.
			            <br/>
			            An Application for <b>Family Coach</b> would
			            be classified as <b>New</b> for that Role.
			        </div>
			    </div>
			
			    <!-- INFO BOX -->
			    <div style='
			        width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;
			        background:#F5F5F5;border-radius:7px;padding:9px 11px;
			    '>
			        <div style='font-size:10px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px;'>
			            How to use this information
			        </div>
			        <div style='font-size:10px;line-height:1.45;color:#555555;'>
			            Understand how much Individual application activity
			            comes from first-time applications for a Role
			            versus Individuals applying again for the same Role.
			            This helps identify recurring approval activity.
			        </div>
			    </div>
			
			    <!-- NOTE -->
			    <div style='
			        margin-top:10px;padding-top:9px;
			        border-top:1px solid #E5E5E5;
			        font-size:10px;line-height:1.4;color:#666666;
			    '>
			        <b>Important:</b> New and Returning describe
			        <b>Applications, not unique Individuals</b>.
			        Returning does not necessarily mean the Individual
			        was previously Approved or Onboarded.
			        <br/>
			        The classification is based on previous entries
			        into Prospective for the same Individual and Role,
			        regardless of Location.
			    </div>
			
			</div>
			"
		displayFolder: HTML
		lineageTag: 15355447-85c1-4839-9ab2-42f336f8d595

	measure '(HTML) Help - Family Applications by Role' =
			
			"
			<div style='
			    width:100%;height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:14px 18px;
			    font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#333333;background:#FFFFFF;
			'>
			
			    <!-- HEADER -->
			    <div style='display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:10px;'>
			        <div style='
			            width:22px;height:22px;flex:0 0 22px;
			            display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
			            background:#F2F2F2;border-radius:50%;
			            font-size:12px;font-weight:700;
			        '>i</div>
			        <div style='font-size:15px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.2;'>
			            Family Applications by Role
			        </div>
			    </div>
			
			    <!-- DESCRIPTION -->
			    <div style='font-size:11px;line-height:1.45;margin-bottom:12px;'>
			        Shows the distribution of <b>Family approval activity
			        by volunteer Role</b>, including Applications,
			        Approvals, and Onboardings recorded during the
			        selected period.
			    </div>
			
			    <!-- METRICS -->
			    <div style='
			        font-size:10px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;
			        letter-spacing:0.5px;color:#666666;margin-bottom:5px;
			    '>
			        What do the columns represent?
			    </div>
			
			    <div style='font-size:11px;line-height:1.5;margin-bottom:12px;'>
			        <b>Role:</b> The volunteer Role associated with
			        the Family approval process.<br/>
			        <b>Applications:</b> Number of Applications initiated
			        during the selected period, based on the date
			        the Family entered <b>Prospective</b>.<br/>
			        <b>Approvals:</b> Number of <b>Approved</b> events
			        recorded during the selected period.<br/>
			        <b>Onboardings:</b> Number of <b>Onboarded</b> events
			        recorded during the selected period.
			    </div>
			
			    <!-- EXAMPLE -->
			    <div style='
			        width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;
			        background:#F5F5F5;border-radius:7px;padding:9px 11px;
			        margin-bottom:10px;
			    '>
			        <div style='font-size:10px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px;'>
			            Example
			        </div>
			        <div style='font-size:10px;line-height:1.45;color:#555555;'>
			            A Family starts a <b>Host Family</b> Application
			            in <b>2025</b> and reaches <b>Onboarded in 2026</b>.
			            <br/>
			            When selecting 2025, the Application is counted
			            under <b>Applications</b>.
			            When selecting 2026, its Onboarding is counted
			            under <b>Onboardings</b>.
			        </div>
			    </div>
			
			    <!-- INFO BOX -->
			    <div style='
			        width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;
			        background:#F5F5F5;border-radius:7px;padding:9px 11px;
			    '>
			        <div style='font-size:10px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px;'>
			            How to use this information
			        </div>
			        <div style='font-size:10px;line-height:1.45;color:#555555;'>
			            Compare approval activity across Family Roles
			            to understand where Applications are being initiated
			            and where Approvals and Onboardings are occurring.
			            Identify changes in activity across reporting periods.
			        </div>
			    </div>
			
			    <!-- NOTE -->
			    <div style='
			        margin-top:10px;padding-top:9px;
			        border-top:1px solid #E5E5E5;
			        font-size:10px;line-height:1.4;color:#666666;
			    '>
			        <b>Important:</b> These columns represent
			        <b>independent events, not a Cohort or conversion funnel</b>.
			        Applications use the Prospective date, Approvals use
			        the Approved date, and Onboardings use the Onboarded date.
			        <br/>
			        An Approval or Onboarding may belong to an Application
			        initiated in an earlier period. Therefore, Onboardings
			        may exceed Applications or Approvals.
			        <br/>
			        Results represent <b>approval activity, not unique Families</b>.
			        Future-dated events are excluded.
			    </div>
			
			</div>
			"
		displayFolder: HTML
		lineageTag: 5333f2ad-d554-4596-91a1-2e923ece42cc

